From 62e16213e41ea0d4fec00da927aa9a951c9aa707 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xavier Geerinck <xavier.geerinck@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:06:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] test(sandbox): cross-app sandbox calls under mTLS

crossapp runs without Sentry, so the same-app rule for reserved internal
actor types never applied there and the ACL change for hosted sandbox types
had only unit tests. crossappmtls runs the same pool and caller apps with
Sentry identities and checks, against the pool app's internal API:
- a caller app of the same namespace execs through its sidecar, and with a
  forged same-namespace identity directly: allowed;
- callers from another namespace (as "caller" and as "pool"): denied;
- a call to another app's sandbox actor type: denied.

With workflow_acl.go as before the ACL change, both allowed cases fail
with PermissionDenied.

The pool daprd gets PATH explicitly: WithSentry leaves daprd an
environment with only the trust anchors, and the process driver looks
commands up in daprd's PATH.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
